From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:02:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] .github: test pull requests merged onto the current base

The checks used the event's base.sha, which GitHub records at a pull
request's last push and a re-run replays, and kernel-pr-check built the
pull request's own commits. A fix merged since a branch was cut never
reached its CI: #43 kept failing on the gs201 schema messages #47 had
already fixed. The job now fetches the base branch when it runs and
passes --merge, so the builds and the device-tree comparison run on the
pull request merged onto that base, and a conflict says "rebase
needed". The commit checks still read only the pull request's commits.

This file is repository tooling, not kernel code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/checks.yml | 19 ++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/checks.yml b/.github/workflows/checks.yml
index c6b6fda88..8d6a06e4d 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/checks.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/checks.yml
@@ -3,9 +3,11 @@
 # CONTRIBUTING.md section 6.2), kept in omarchy-mobile beside the tool it
 # runs (ci/linux-omarchy-mobile/checks.yml, tools/kernel-pr-check). It
 # checks out the pull request's commits and omarchy-mobile's tools, then
-# runs the sign-off, prefix, checkpatch and identifier checks and the W=1,
-# dtbs_check and dt_binding_check builds, comparing device-tree warnings
-# with the base. Not kernel code: never part of an upstream submission.
+# runs the sign-off, prefix, checkpatch and identifier checks on its
+# commits, and the W=1, dtbs_check and dt_binding_check builds on the pull
+# request merged onto the current base (--merge), comparing device-tree
+# warnings with that base. Not kernel code: never part of an upstream
+# submission.
 name: checks
 
 on:
@@ -30,8 +32,11 @@ jobs:
           path: linux
           fetch-depth: 0
           ref: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}
-      - name: The base
-        run: git -C linux fetch --no-tags origin "${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}"
+      # The base branch as it is when the job runs, not the event's base.sha:
+      # that is recorded at the pull request's last push, and a re-run
+      # replays it, so a fix merged since then would never be seen.
+      - name: The base, now
+        run: git -C linux fetch --no-tags origin "+refs/heads/${{ github.event.pull_request.base.ref }}:refs/remotes/origin/base"
       - uses: actions/checkout@v5
         with:
           repository: derekross/omarchy-mobile
@@ -43,5 +48,5 @@ jobs:
           pip install --break-system-packages dtschema
       - name: tools/kernel-pr-check
         run: |
-          omarchy-mobile/tools/kernel-pr-check -C linux --build "$RUNNER_TEMP/kbuild" \
-            "${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}" "${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}"
+          omarchy-mobile/tools/kernel-pr-check -C linux --build "$RUNNER_TEMP/kbuild" --merge \
+            origin/base "${{ github.event.pull_request.head.sha }}"
